        "pista": {
          "evento": {
            "nome": "Road blocked",
            "fala": [
              "Some guys just cut you off. Not Pista crew — outsiders testing the new gang.",
              "Ambush at the corner. Half a dozen waiting for you to walk by, just to run their mouths.",
              "The street narrowed all of a sudden and some tougher kids cut your path. They want to see if you're bone or paper."
            ]
          },
          "chegada": [
            "This is the Pista, kid. The asphalt down below — the root of it all.",
            "Everybody worth something today crawled on this ground first. The Patchwork started here. Alan, elsewhere, started from zero just like you. Now it's your turn to prove you're not just another face.",
            "Take the kids' spots, get your name running mouth to mouth. When the whole Pista knows you exist, Coal comes down out of the dark to face you — and that's when you find out if you've got what it takes.",
            "Move. Touch whatever's lighting up."
          ],
          "sinal": {
            "nome": "The stoplight corner",
            "sub": "kid selling candy, sharp eyes on everything",
            "fala": [
              "Hey, you with the new gang? Came down to the Pista alone, no crew behind you. Either you're brave or you're stupid — I'll know real soon.",
              "We don't just sell candy here, man. We sell what we see from this light. And we see EVERYTHING that moves on this block. Want to know something? Trade a word — or trade some cash."
            ],
            "escolhas": {
              "compra": {
                "label": "Buy the candy and hear what he saw",
                "resultado": "He closes his fist on the change without even counting it. \"The junkyard right up ahead. Old padlock, easy to crack. Inside there's scrap worth real money — and whatever the owner left before he vanished off the Pista for good.\""
              },
              "aperta": {
                "label": "Lean on the kid so he talks for free",
                "resultado": [
                  "The kid backs off but doesn't run. \"Ugh, now it's really gone bad. Should've bought the candy.\"",
                  "\"You lean on a kid like that and then want respect? Not happening.\" He whistles — and he's not alone."
                ]
              },
              "ignora": {
                "label": "Ignore him and keep climbing",
                "resultado": "You walk past without even a glance. The kid spits and burns your face into memory — information's a currency too, and now he owes you one. There's a junkyard up ahead."
              }
            }
          },
          "ferro": {
            "nome": "The junkyard",
            "sub": "locked gate, a secret kept inside",
            "intro": "The gate's just a chain with a combination lock — nothing a trained hand can't handle. The crew watches the pins turn once, then it's memorize the sequence and repeat it without a shake. Slip a hand and the guard wakes up and the game turns into a fight on the spot."
          },
          "beco": {
            "nome": "Rasteira's alley",
            "sub": "a Rato de Pista spot",
            "fala": [
              "This alley's Rato de Pista, pal. We don't want to climb, don't want your turf, don't want to own anything — we just don't want to get stepped on. And a fresh gang coming down here thinking it owns the street... this one gets stepped on, no tears.",
              "Well, look who's here. Fresh little crew thinking the Pista's a playground.",
              "This face again? Maybe this time you learn."
            ]
          },
          "rinha": {
            "nome": "The back-alley pit",
            "sub": "clandestine betting",
            "fala": "Betting ring at the back of the alley, kid. You step in, you eat it or you cash out. There's always some nutcase wanting to test their hand against the fresh gang — come on, take it as many times as you can stay standing."
          },
          "birosca": {
            "nome": "Old Nato's bar",
            "sub": "the corner elder — the only grown-up on the Pista you can trust",
            "fala": [
              "Sit, kid. Have some mate. You're climbing way too fast for someone nobody around here knows by name.",
              "I know where Coal hides when he vanishes into the dark. I'll tell you, no runaround. But first do me a run — take a package across without the patrol car's beam catching your trail.",
              "Handle that and the Pista starts to respect you, not just fear you. And the bar keeps its door open for your crew to rest whenever it needs to."
            ],
            "escolhas": {
              "aceita_corre": {
                "label": "Take Nato's run",
                "resultado": "\"Done, kid. Package is behind the counter. And a bonus: Rasteira's other spot is right up to the right.\""
              },
              "so_papo": {
                "label": "Just want the information",
                "resultado": "\"Stubborn, huh. Then straight to the bone: Rasteira's other spot is up there. Lock both down and Coal shows up on his own, wanting to know who you are.\""
              }
            }
          },
          "informante": {
            "nome": "Duda, the Ear",
            "sub": "knows everything that moves in Marélia before it's a rumor",
            "fala": [
              "Hey, back on the Pista? That's what this block is: everything that happens in Marélia passes through here before it's even corner gossip. And I hear ALL of it, kid.",
              "There's something going on over at the Feira the folks there won't tell you for free. The Collector's lying low, waiting for the right moment to show."
            ],
            "escolhas": {
              "perguntar": {
                "label": "Ask about the Feira",
                "resultado": "\"The Collector only comes out of hiding once he knows his enforcers already took a beating. Go to the Feira, handle the spots — then come back if you need more intel.\""
              }
            }
          },
          "corre": {
            "nome": "Nato's run",
            "sub": "carry the package without the patrol car seeing",
            "intro": "Cross the block with the package without stepping into the patrol car's beam — one wrong turn and it's a sure fight with a badge. The crew spreads out and covers your move. It's the price of Nato's information, and also the price of peace here on the Pista."
          },
          "beco_2": {
            "nome": "Rasteira's other spot",
            "fala": "You again? Took the alley down there and already figured the whole Pista would kneel for the fresh gang. Changes hands every week here, man — but not for whoever shows up thinking they own a corner on day one."
          },
          "descanso": {
            "nome": "Rest at the bar",
            "sub": "mate, bread and quiet",
            "intro": "Some time sitting, out of the hot street sun, in Nato's bar. Costs a little change, but it patches the crew up and everyone comes back whole — hurt, nobody wins a fight."
          },
          "descanso_2": {
            "nome": "The cousin's corner bar",
            "sub": "on the other side of the wall",
            "intro": "Nato's cousin runs a makeshift bar over on this side. Same deal: pay a little change and the crew sorts itself out before heading into Carvão's warehouse."
          },
          "posmuro_1": {
            "nome": "The watchdogs",
            "fala": ["\"You lost your mind coming here, huh?\" Carvão's first crew blocks the way.", "Two heavy dealers smoking on the warehouse steps. They spot you and spit on the ground."]
          },
          "posmuro_2": {
            "nome": "The block manager",
            "fala": ["Carvão's right hand in person, with an escort. \"Past the wall, you come in by invitation. Were you invited?\"", "This one doesn't run. Folds his arms, signals the goons: \"handle it.\""]
          },
          "loja": {
            "nome": "Pista Shop"
          },
          "achado": {
            "nome": "The back of the junkyard",
            "sub": "what the owner left behind",
            "linha": "Behind a pile of scrap, a forgotten crate: some change and iron that still works. Nobody will miss it — the owner's long gone, vanished off the Pista, and nobody asks why."
          },
          "rasteira_velha": {
            "nome": "Old Rasteira",
            "sub": "the alley's owner in person",
            "fala": [
              "You beat the kids and already figured the Pista was yours? I trained every one of these punks with my own hands. Face me first — then Coal comes down to see you up close.",
              "Trained every one of these kids with these hands. Come see what's left to teach you.",
              "Back? Good. Now I get to teach it again, with more feeling."
            ]
          },
          "oficina": {
            "nome": "Nando's workshop",
            "sub": "Mr. Nando fixes what the street breaks",
            "fala": [
              "Look at the fresh little gang already working the spots. Let me tell you something, kid: to face Coal you need iron in your hand, not just chest.",
              "Bring me two pieces of scrap from that junkyard — one you pull cracking the lock, the other's hidden in the back. Bring them and I'll forge you a piece on the spot for your crew.",
              "And as a bonus I'll drop where Coal hides when he vanishes into the dark. That's worth more than any weapon, kid. We got a deal?"
            ],
            "escolhas": {
              "forjar": {
                "label": "Hand over the scrap and take the piece",
                "resultado": "Nando hammers a while, blows off the smoke and passes you a still-warm tin knuckle. \"Coal parks deep in Rasteira's alley, behind the wall. Vanishes in the dark, but always to the same corner — a crook always repeats a pattern. Now go up and get him.\""
              }
            }
          },
          "beco_3": {
            "nome": "The third spot",
            "sub": "another piece of Rato de Pista",
            "fala": "You people don't quit, huh? The Pista's got spots like bullet holes — there's always one more hidden in some corner. This one's mine. Come prove you're worth it, or go back where you came from."
          },
          "sinaleiro": {
            "nome": "The Head Signalman",
            "sub": "if he whistles, the whole block runs",
            "fala": [
              "I run the eyes of the whole Pista, kid. Every lookout, every signal, every runner at the light answers to my whistle. You got past all of them without anyone whistling — but you don't get past me. With me it's different.",
              "I whistle, the whole block runs to help. Who do you whistle to?",
              "Thought it'd be easy the second time? Wrong, kid."
            ]
          },
